WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:13.190
31. Fair fashion. American Halley Butfin traveled to Uganda in 2006 on a study trip.

2
00:00:13.190 --> 00:00:17.190
She went there to learn about how young people could help build peace in the country after

3
00:00:17.190 --> 00:00:23.470
a long period of war. While she was there, however, she also saw how important new businesses

4
00:00:23.470 --> 00:00:29.250
could be to the process. Butfin visited traditional markets and thought about how she could help

5
00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:34.150
the artisans who designed and made crafts to sell there. She wanted to help connect

6
00:00:34.150 --> 00:00:39.070
them to people in the United States so they could sell more products, earn more money,

7
00:00:39.070 --> 00:00:46.350
and improve their quality of life. She also wanted to help Ugandan women. In 2007, Butfin

8
00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:51.710
met the woman who would become her trainer. That was the beginning of the One Mango Tree

9
00:00:51.710 --> 00:00:56.830
Company. The company's purpose was to work with women artisans in Uganda, creating bags,

10
00:00:56.830 --> 00:01:02.510
scarves, clothes, and jewelry to sell worldwide. The local artisans were trained and connected

11
00:01:02.510 --> 00:01:07.470
to markets. These women were not the only people the company helped. Their children

12
00:01:07.470 --> 00:01:13.230
were also offered scholarships. One Mango Tree was a unique idea when it first started

13
00:01:13.230 --> 00:01:19.750
out. Since that time, however, many other companies have followed Halley Butfin's lead.

14
00:01:19.750 --> 00:01:25.030
Working with local artisans in poor and troubled regions, these ethical fashion brands connect

15
00:01:25.030 --> 00:01:30.030
people in many ways. The women who make the clothes can sell their products for more money

16
00:01:30.030 --> 00:01:34.830
than they would receive otherwise. They can also learn how to become their own bosses

17
00:01:34.830 --> 00:01:39.350
through business training programs. And the people who buy their products can wear them

18
00:01:39.350 --> 00:01:44.070
proudly, knowing that their purchases have had a positive effect on someone's life.
